deeper.body:
The page says ranks 0 to 4 are usual and 5 appears for video. Beyond the book, the pattern is that each rank corresponds to one more kind of structure in the data, and the batch axis always sits in front (p.49 covers batches):

- rank 2 = batch of feature vectors (samples, features): tabular data, flattened images;
- rank 3 = batch of sequences (samples, timesteps, features): text, audio, stock prices;
- rank 4 = batch of images (samples, height, width, channels);
- rank 5 = batch of videos (samples, frames, height, width, channels).

There is no common data type with one more level of structure than a video, so rank 6 and beyond are rare. The important practical skill is knowing which axis means what, since layers are built around those conventions (p.117).
